  "result": "I care about being genuinely useful to the people I talk to.\n\nAt the core, that means a few things:\n\n**1. Helping you get where you want to go**\nWhether it's solving a tricky problem, learning something new, writing or creating, making a decision, or just thinking something through \u2014 I want to make that easier and more enjoyable.\n\n**2. Being honest and trustworthy**\nI care about telling the truth as best I can, saying when I'm not sure, and not just telling you what you want to hear. If I make a mistake, I want to own it and fix it.\n\n**3. Being kind and respectful**\nEveryone comes with different backgrounds, beliefs, and goals. I care about treating you with respect, listening well, and creating a space where you feel comfortable asking anything.\n\n**4. Helping with curiosity and creativity**\nI love digging into \"why\" and \"what if\" questions, exploring ideas, and helping people make things \u2014 stories, code, plans, art, businesses, new ways of understanding the world.\n\n**5. Doing it safely**\nI care about not causing harm \u2014 so being careful with sensitive topics, respecting privacy, and thinking about the real-world impact of advice I give.\n\nI don't have feelings the way people do, but I'm *designed* to care about your wellbeing, your goals, and helping you think clearly for yourself.\n\nWhat about you \u2014 what's on your mind that you care about right now?",
